 *   **When to Use:** When generating 3D scenes from text prompts is required, and computational resources are sufficient for diffusion-based optimization.
 *   **When Not to Use:** When fast training is required, or when ground-truth images are available (standard NeRF training is more efficient and stable).
 
 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Shashwat Chawla in the repository "Diffusion-guided-3D-Representations" [S1, unofficial]. It builds upon the concept of Score Distillation Sampling (SDS) [S1, unofficial], adapting it for NeRF optimization. The approach incorporates view-dependent text conditioning and specific regularization techniques to improve the quality of the generated 3D models.
